# Initialization

Read in this order. Stop at step 3 unless the task needs more.

## 1. Always

- `AGENTS.md` - mandatory AI disclosure and summary style.
- `.claude/new-chat-template.md` - start here: the FILL IN block (pull
  request, task, deferred notes, decisions), the standing rules, the
  records, the checks and the process for one fix.

## 2. Then run

- `python -B maintenances/_repo/_maintenance/tools/orient.py` - the
  current state from this checkout: open ledger, the pull request's
  fragments, each area's next finding id and next action. Exit 1 means a
  record could not be read; say so before anything else.

## 3. By task (read only what the task touches)

Maintenance of a submodule or the repository:
- `maintenances/MAINTAINING.md` - the one read order for maintenance work
  (the map, the engineering rules, the fresh-chat handoff, the owning
  area's records and skill). Follow it; it is not repeated here.

Notes and release notes:
- `upcoming_changes/README.md` - how a ledger note is written and closed.
- `docs/source/whats_new/upcoming_changes/README.md` - fragment sections,
  types and the one-bullet rule.

Skills, agents and plugins:
- `plugins/INDEX.md` - generated index of skills and agents by package.
- `plugins/README.md` - how plugins are built and shipped (long; read the
  part the task needs).

## Delivery

- `python -B maintenances/_repo/_maintenance/tools/deliver.py OLD NEW NAME --out DIR`
  - patch and drop-in zip, both proved to turn OLD into NEW.
